 ## Overview
-The Structural Similarity Index (SSIM) measures the perceived distortion between a rendered image and a ground truth image by comparing local patterns of pixel intensities, assuming the human visual system is highly adapted to structured natural scene information [S1, unofficial][S3]. It serves as a standard benchmark for image quality in radiance-field optimization, complementing pixel-wise metrics like MSE and PSNR [S2, unofficial][S3]. Unlike MSE, which treats all errors equally, SSIM accounts for luminance, contrast, and structural correlations, providing a value between -1 and 1 where 1 indicates identical images [S2, unofficial].
